mtk-vcodec: decoder: keep displayed buffers with userspace.

When vpud releases a frame buffer, get_free_buffer() re-queued it to the
decoder if it was never returned to userspace. The test used the
queued_in_vb2/queued_in_v4l2 flags, which are only cleared when userspace
dequeues the buffer, so a frame already marked done for display but not yet
dequeued was handed back to the decoder too. The hardware then decoded the
next picture into a buffer userspace was about to read: clients that do not
dequeue immediately (GStreamer, FFmpeg) saw torn and out-of-order frames.

Skip buffers that were reported for display; they return to the decoder
when userspace queues them again.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/mtk-vcodec/mtk_vcodec_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/mtk-vcodec/mtk_vcodec_dec.c
@@ -240,8 +240,11 @@
 				free_frame_buffer->index, free_frame_buffer->fb_base[i].dmabuf);
 		}
 		dstbuf->used = false;
+		/* A displayed buffer belongs to userspace until it is queued
+		 * again; never hand it back to the decoder from here. */
 		if ((dstbuf->queued_in_vb2) &&
 			(dstbuf->queued_in_v4l2) &&
+			!dstbuf->ready_to_display &&
 			(free_frame_buffer->status == FB_ST_FREE)) {
 			/*
